{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508292-vestiges-of-the-hunt-or-ghosts-of-siskur-dahs-past","id":508292,"title":"Vestiges of the Hunt, or Ghosts of Siskur-Dahs Past","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-08T12:42:05-07:00","id":508292,"title":"Vestiges of the Hunt, or Ghosts of Siskur-Dahs Past","content":"'These were the remnants of Khoonbish's victims, and he'd scattered them like breadcrumbs to mark his trail through the spirit realm. It was a paltry entourage compared to others I'd seen, but they still stretched like a flight of migratory blackbirds from the Mediterranean Sea's Eastern Basin to the Palestinian coast and across the Middle East.'<br /> - The Lineage<br /> <br /> One of the things that's come up in a few pieces of werewolf media, perhaps most famously in the American Werewolf series, is the idea that those who a werewolf kills don't get their eternal rest. Instead they spend their days following the werewolf until it is put down. In some cases they urge this, trying to encourage or trick confused werewolves into suicide. Other times they silently judge, or act as a sort of entourage or both, howling alongside the werewolf on its hunt and whispering in its ear what a horrible creature it is. And sometimes it just leaves a swarm of ghosts, anchored to the werewolf but unable to do anything to act against it.<br /> <br /> So, if you were to incorporate this into Werewolf second edition, how would you do it? Would you limit it to victims of the Siskur-Dah? Have it depend on some sort of spectral gift being unlocked, or perhaps a Wolf Gift werewolves are normally spared from? Would they be full fledged ghosts? Again, providing you wanted to see something like that in the game, how would you like to see it done?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T18:25:53-07:00","id":508606,"title":"","content":"Just going off of first impressions of the concept, I'd draw on the bits of 1e about the state of the werewolf soul, the disconnect between the Shadow and the Underworld, and the unihar's old role as the classical definition of a nemesis \u2014 sometimes the Uratha trip some bit of arcane causality in the course of their existence that spawns or summons a spirit that incorporates those who fall to the werewolf's claws and jaws into a bow wave of preemptive retribution that only ends with the death of the Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T18:36:28-07:00","id":508613,"title":"","content":"In Book of the Dead, there were merits that could simulate the latter, at least if the character was hunting Man or the People. For the others, forcing Shards or Spirits into Fetishes seems to be the only remotely feasible way to do so, short hacking Harmony to shoehorn vestiges of that sort into the system maths. It also makes more sense for Tribes that have connections to the dead or war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T18:47:40-07:00","id":508617,"title":"","content":"Something different happens to someone when a werewolf kills them in <i>kuruth.</i><br /> <br /> They call it Death Rage for a reason, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T18:53:45-07:00","id":508620,"title":"","content":"What happens to shards when they die, anyways? Or werewolves for that matter? As Satchel pointed out they don't follow the normal route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T23:11:19-07:00","id":508776,"title":"","content":"'Ghosts' of prey that has been improperly hunted haunting those who slew them sounds rather interesting.<br /> Not actual ghosts, at least not as defined in the game. When you slay a claimed or a host or spirit it doesn't leave an echo of a human soul behind. But an echo, an ephemeral reflection of a reflection, that has potential.<br /> I wouldn't let such a thing interact directly with anything, maybe some social stuff. Most certainly no combat. Want to get rid of it? Give the prey it's due.<br /> <br /> Ni Dana: respect the prey. There is a reason some Hunts are Sacred.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'd do it in much the same way a 'normal/muggle' mortal would deal with a ghost in a classic ghost story. The offending wolf sees the slain Azlu out of their eye, distracting them at a crucial moment. The Red Talon spots a trail left by a Predator King with help from a shattered spirit of a car. No matter where you go, you can feel that damned sheriff's eyes on you, even though you ate his heart a week ago.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, sounds like some of it could be modeled by Conditions rather than game stats. That fits nicely with the idea of half-spirit creatures being haunted by 'dead' spirits, opposed to the spirits of the dead. Although an Aspect of a 'dark' Gift, (maybe for Bale Hounds 2nd ed), collecting these emeninations and inflicting your 'Prey Conditions' upon them sounds kind of neat.<br /> <i>&quot;If you had noticed me eating your human kin earlier, I wouldn't have needed to send their shattered souls after you. Still, you're at the Wound now and that's what matters, eh Viruhk-Ur? Oh, you two haven't met yet! Let me introduce you...&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 05-09-2015, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T17:21:38-07:00","id":515615,"title":"","content":"And now I am reminded of old Korean stories, where people killed and eaten by tigers become specters that haunt and are enslaved by the tiger. The ghosts then lead the tiger to their next, easy meal of human, starting with the ghosts' own living family members.<br /> <br /> Maybe when werewolves eat humans/wolves/werewolves for Essence, and completely drain spirits of their Essence to perma-kill them, the victims rise as similiar ghosts? Oh, our peninsula didn't have prominent stories about wolves thanks to all those tigers in the past, but then again, an Urshul could be mistaken for any large predator under Lunacy......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5789-acanthus","name":"acanthus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T22:06:33-07:00","id":515828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>acanthus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508292-vestiges-of-the-hunt-or-ghosts-of-siskur-dahs-past?p=515615#post515615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now I am reminded of old Korean stories, where people killed and eaten by tigers become specters that haunt and are enslaved by the tiger. The ghosts then lead the tiger to their next, easy meal of human, starting with the ghosts' own living family members.<br /> <br /> Maybe when werewolves eat humans/wolves/werewolves for Essence, and completely drain spirits of their Essence to perma-kill them, the victims rise as similiar ghosts? Oh, our peninsula didn't have prominent stories about wolves thanks to all those tigers in the past, but then again, an Urshul could be mistaken for any large predator under Lunacy......</div> </div> </div> </div>Skin-Thief Facet. Tigers are way more formidable than wolves, specially where they are far more predominant predators.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}